From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Frank Li <frankli@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 4 Jun 2026 04:10:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm: sunxi-hdmi: read default HPD mask from DTS

The DRM HDMI driver exposes a runtime hpd_mask sysfs knob, but it does
not read the matching DTS property during initialization. Allow board
DTS files to set the same default value when a board needs a stable HPD
policy at boot.

---
 bsp/drivers/drm/sunxi_drm_hdmi.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/bsp/drivers/drm/sunxi_drm_hdmi.c b/bsp/drivers/drm/sunxi_drm_hdmi.c
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/bsp/drivers/drm/sunxi_drm_hdmi.c
+++ b/bsp/drivers/drm/sunxi_drm_hdmi.c
@@ -2961,6 +2961,9 @@ static int __sunxi_hdmi_init_dts(struct sunxi_drm_hdmi *hdmi)
 	ret = of_property_read_u32(node, "hdmi_ddc_index", &value);
 	hdmi->hdmi_ctrl.drv_dts_ddc_index = (ret != 0x0) ? 0x1F : value;
 
+	ret = of_property_read_u32(node, "hdmi_hpd_mask", &value);
+	hdmi->hdmi_ctrl.drv_hpd_mask = (ret != 0x0) ? 0x0 : value;
+
 	/* parse tcon clock */
 	pclk->clk_tcon_tv = devm_clk_get(dev, "clk_tcon_tv");
 	if (IS_ERR_OR_NULL(pclk->clk_tcon_tv))
-- 
2.43.0
